-- title:
--   Quadratic relation passes to products of Tate modules
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a field $k$ that is an algebra over $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$ and for which the coordinate ring $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,k$ modulo the ideal generated by $\mathrm{drinfeldPoly} - 1$ is a domain; let $F$ be its fraction field `drinfeldFunctionField q k`, and let $H =$ `hSubgroup q` be the kernel of `hChar q`, i.e. the subgroup of pairs $(g,\alpha) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q) \times \mathrm{GF}(q^2)^\times$ with $\det(g)\,\alpha^{q+1} = 1$. Fix a prime $\ell$, a field $E$ over $\mathbb{Q}_\ell$, a type $S$, a character $\theta \colon \mathrm{GF}(q^2)^\times \to E^\times$, and a representation $\sigma$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ on an $E$-vector space $W$. Write $V_E = E \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}_\ell} \bigl(\mathbb{Q}_\ell \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\ell} T_\ell\bigr)$, where $T_\ell$ is the Tate module of the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of $F$ over $k$, with the $H$-action `tateRep` obtained from the action of $H$ on $F$ by $k$-algebra automorphisms. Assume: for every $E$-linear $u \colon W \to V_E$ satisfying $u \circ \sigma(g) = \mathrm{tateRep}(g,1) \circ u$ for all $g$ with $(g,1) \in H$, and for all $(g,\alpha) \in H$, the operator $A(v) = \mathrm{tateRep}(g,\alpha) \circ v \circ \sigma(g^{-1})$ satisfies $A(A(u)) - (\theta(\alpha) + \theta(\alpha^q))\,A(u) + \theta(\alpha)\theta(\alpha^q)\,u = 0$. Then the same statement holds with $V_E$ replaced by the $S$-indexed product $\mathrm{tateProd} = (S \to V_E)$, carrying the componentwise $H$-action `tateProdRep`.
--
--   The quadratic relation expresses that, on $H$-equivariant maps from $\sigma$ into the Tate module, the operator attached to $(g,\alpha)$ satisfies the characteristic polynomial of the pair $\{\theta(\alpha), \theta(\alpha^q)\}$; this lemma transports that relation from one copy of the Tate module of the Drinfeld curve to an arbitrary product of copies with the diagonal action. It is used in the identification of the inertia labels of a newform whose associated representation is cuspidal of the given type.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_tateProdRep_quadratic_of_forall.lean

